sequenceDiagram
  %% status: draft
  %% command: process:stop
  %% kind: process.stop
  %% Proposed ADR 0271 path. Names below describe resource effects; primitive names are settled with the implementation.
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>Orbit caller
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>admission
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as Target Node<br/>executor
  CLI->>GW: process:stop PROCESS
  Note over GW: Check access and target
  alt plain host systemd unit and every target advertises support
    GW->>EN: Admit engine Operation
    GW-->>CLI: Operation accepted
    %%> The kind must be enabled. Admission selects one owner for the full Operation.
    EN->>N: Apply stopped state<br/>and disable at boot
    %%> Read back inactive and disabled. An already-stopped unit may still need its boot policy changed.
    %%> Keep Docker, Instance-container, production-specific and Vite plans on their existing paths until their end checks have coverage.
    N-->>EN: Observed unit state
    alt verified receipt
      EN->>GW: Record Process stopped
    else signed step failed
      EN->>GW: Record the failed step
    else receipt missing
      Note over EN: Recover the signed step
      %%> A missing receipt allows redelivery for the same Operation step. Recover its journaled result or verify the owned state before settlement. A deterministic refusal records the failed step; retain the domain's existing failure state.
    end
  else unsupported Node plan
    Note over GW: Use existing Process flow
    %%> Decide before dispatch. An accepted engine Operation keeps its owner through recovery.
  end
